-- title:
--   Normalised order on a DVR: additivity, non-negativity, units, uniformisers
-- statement:
--   Let $O$ be a commutative domain that is a discrete valuation ring and let $L$ be a field which is an $O$-algebra and a fraction field of $O$ (both in the same universe). For $a \in L$, $\operatorname{addOrd}$ is defined to be $0$ when $a = 0$ and otherwise $-\operatorname{toAdd}$ of the nonzero value at $a$ of the $\mathbb{Z}^{m0}$-valued adic valuation attached to the height-one prime `maximalSpectrum O` given by the maximal ideal of $O$; so it is the normalised additive order, with the convention $\operatorname{addOrd}(0)=0$. The theorem asserts the conjunction of four statements: (i) for all nonzero $a, b \in L$, $\operatorname{addOrd}(ab) = \operatorname{addOrd}(a) + \operatorname{addOrd}(b)$; (ii) for every $x \in O$, $\operatorname{addOrd}$ of the image of $x$ in $L$ is $\ge 0$; (iii) for every nonzero $x \in O$, that order vanishes if and only if $x$ is a unit of $O$; and (iv) for every discrete valuation domain $R'$ in the same universe equipped with an $R'$-algebra structure on $O$ whose structure map is a local homomorphism, if the ideal of $O$ generated by the image of the maximal ideal of $R'$ equals the maximal ideal of $O$, then for every $\pi \in R'$ with maximal ideal of $R'$ equal to $\operatorname{span}\{\pi\}$ one has $\operatorname{addOrd}$ of the image of $\pi$ in $L$ equal to $1$.
--
--   These are the basic properties of the normalised valuation $\operatorname{ord}$ on the fraction field of a discrete valuation ring, in the form used to measure the order of a top differential form along a discrete valuation ring; the fourth clause records that a uniformiser of an unramified (index-one) discrete valuation subring is again a uniformiser, so has order $1$. The bundle is used in the study of orders of top forms under base change, in [`NeronModelInfra.TopFormOrder.le_ord_and_ord_eq_iff_bijective_mapBaseChange_of_eq_unit_mul_zpow_smul`](thm.html#NeronModelInfra.TopFormOrder.le_ord_and_ord_eq_iff_bijective_mapBaseChange_of_eq_unit_mul_zpow_smul) and [`NeronModelInfra.TopFormOrder.ord_topFormMap_eq_ord_of_map_maximalIdeal_eq`](thm.html#NeronModelInfra.TopFormOrder.ord_topFormMap_eq_ord_of_map_maximalIdeal_eq).
